    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d809">

                <pb facs="1570" n="1530" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v09p1/pg1530"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">684A.85/4–2554: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 809<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Egypt (Caffery) to the
                        Department of State</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d809-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-04-25T14:00:00+02:00">April 25, 1954—2 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1348. Re Tel Aviv telegram 1071.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d809-f2"/> Riad told
                    Embassy officer yesterday he or Gohar prepared meet Israelis opposite number any
                    time for informal discussion border problems with or without local commanders
                    and police participation and in presence UN observer. <pb facs="1571" n="1531"
                        xml:id="pg1531"/> Riad said such meetings had been suggested many times,
                    most recently to MAC chairman Hinkle who approved, but fact that nothing ever
                    came of suggestions showed Israelis seek political or propaganda advantage from
                    border situation and have no genuine desire reduce incidents. Nevertheless,
                    Egypt always prepared cooperate immediately in any such meeting.</p>
                <p>Israeli concept of purpose such meeting as described reference telegram was not
                    conveyed to Riad.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
